{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c4b7","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a08946-5fbe-7830-b2e8-af2616179f48"},"sequence":182,"recorded_at":1780531400000359,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"b6e8a9ed-35e9-4191-9a50-1dfe1ff8a38f","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"b6e8a9ed-35e9-4191-9a50-1dfe1ff8a38f","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"b6e8a9ed-35e9-4191-9a50-1dfe1ff8a38f"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a08946-b6e3-7030-9745-6a3b514d7892"},"task_id":"01a08946-b6e3-7030-9745-6a3b514d7892","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a08946-b6e3-7030-9745-6a3b514d7892","chunk":"Read text file `/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.temp/resources/TASK-260909-2ez769/TASK-260909-2ez769_review-verdict-rev3.md`.\n1|# CR revision 3 review — changes requested\n2|\n3|Task TASK-260909-2ez769; CR-TASK-260909-2ez769-3 revision 3.\n4|Base a89328ca85a613abde39660f4be749a8fcf57903; candidate tree\n5|881fb127162ee55a0175313850b4704f41cb24e0. Review is read-only against the\n6|managed worktree. Probes and overlays ran in an archive of the immutable tree\n7|under .temp/TASK-260909-2ez769/review3. No commits or product edits.\n8|\n9|## Blocking findings\n10|\n11|1. **P1: stale mutation authorization is admitted.**\n12|   `internal/hosttrust/authorize.go:191`, `WithMutationAuthorization`, replaces\n13|   the request generation with current.Generation and never compares the\n14|   original binding. `TestReviewerStaleMutation` opens an authorized fixture,\n15|   commits a config authorization generation change, then submits the original\n16|   request. It returns nil and invokes the side-effect callback. Exit 1.\n17|   Section 11.10.3 expressly forbids refreshing a cached number to authorize\n18|   old prepared work. Refuse stale requests before entering the boundary;\n19|   require fresh connection/replanning through the RPC caller contract. Add a\n20|   negative test and a narrowing mutant for this mutation path, not only the\n21|   dispatch generation guard.\n22|\n23|2. **P1: revocation succeeds during an authorized mutation boundary.**\n24|   `internal/hosttrust/lock_unix.go:60-73` uses flock on the same open descriptor\n25|   for all goroutines of a Store, without process-local serialization.\n26|   `TestReviewerRevocationDuringBoundary` waits until the production mutation\n27|   callback is held, then calls Revoke on that Store. Revoke returns success\n28|   before the callback is released. Exit 1 on darwin/arm64.\n29|   The existing `TestMutationAuthorizationSerializesWithRevocation` uses an\n30|   immediate nonblocking select after starting the revocation goroutine; it\n31|   does not give that goroutine time to attempt the lock and misses the bug.\n32|   Implement safe local and cross-process locking, including nested reads and\n33|   concurrent lock initialization; test deterministic boundary contention.\n34|   Section 11.10.3 forbids this success ordering.\n35|\n36|3. **P1: config replacement and generation commit are not crash-atomic.**\n37|   `internal/config/migration_v4_apply.go:82` installs configuration inside\n38|   `CommitConfigChange`; `internal/hosttrust/transact.go:87` commits trust only\n39|   after the callback. Recovery is an in-process error handler, with no durable\n40|   joint transaction/restart marker. `TestReviewerCrashBetweenConfigAndGeneration`\n41|   drives production apply with an OS filesystem wrapper and terminates the\n42|   child process with exit 77 immediately after the real config rename. On\n43|   restart, production Load accepts Config4 and a freshly opened Store accepts\n44|   the old generation (3). The parent test fails, exit 1. No synthetic trust\n45|   bytes or fake decoder are used. This is a process-crash ordering test, not a\n46|   power-loss filesystem test. Sections 6.6 and 11.10.3 require the coherent\n47|   committed config/trust transaction. Add durable recovery/selection and\n48|   corresponding apply/rollback crash tests. Also move current-preview/source/\n49|   generation revalidation into the shared transaction: presently those checks\n50|   precede lock acquisition, leaving a concurrent-change window. The latter\n51|   window is code-inspection evidence, not a separately executed probe.\n52|\n53|4. **P1: native Windows custody is not implemented to its required contract.**\n54|   `internal/hosttrust/custody_windows.go:11-42` requests only owner SID and\n55|   equates it with owner-only access. Ownership does not establish DACL grants;\n56|   no DACL is read or installed. Common permission checks additionally apply\n57|   Unix 0700/0600 tests before this function, without a Windows ACL abstraction.\n58|   Sections 11.10.2 and the explicit native-Windows platform lanes require\n59|   equivalent owner-only ACLs. A successful cross-build and an absent Windows\n60|   runner cannot waive the implementation requirement. Implement and validate\n61|   ACL custody (positive owner-only and negative other-principal access/reparse\n62|   cases). No Windows execution was performed here; actual Windows runtime\n63|   acceptance/refusal remains unverified, not claimed as observed leakage.\n64|\n65|5. **P2: no-secret replication and complete negative-coverage claims exceed evidence.**\n66|   `ExcludedFromReplication` has no production consumer; its only caller is\n67|   `TestExcludedFromReplication`. `TestNoSecretReplication` walks the local\n68|   custody directory and asserts file placement; it does not drive replication,\n69|   snapshot, clone, Session Directory or diagnostic export. No actual secret\n70|   leak is claimed, but the mandatory exclusion is not established at those\n71|   entry points. Provide production enforcement/negative tests or an explicit\n72|   scoped ownership handoff for unavailable surfaces; do not count a returned\n73|   path list as end-to-end exclusion. The config `v4-explicit-label` mutant\n74|   changes only the error identity while retaining refusal: its kill proves\n75|   label precision, not a narrowed semantic admission gate. Correct the claim\n76|   of four config narrowing kills to three semantic plants plus one label plant.\n77|\n78|## Independently derived AC accounting\n79|\n80|**18 of 21 functional AC rows driven**, including three rows with failing\n81|reviewer counterexamples. This is a functional decomposition of sections 6.6,\n82|11.10.2 and 11.10.3 within this leaf, not a claim of all normative clauses or\n83|all gate mutants covered. Fifteen rows have bounded passing test evidence;\n84|three rows below lack the required production proof. The producer's unlisted\n85|21/21 does not establish complete acceptance.\n86|\n87|| # | Scoped row | Production call / named test | Result or bound |\n88||---|---|---|---|\n89||1|Closed Config4|Decode / TestDecodeConfiguration4Refusals|Driven, passes|\n90||2|Historical compatibility and explicit migration|Migrate / TestMigrateRefusesV4Target, TestMigrateRefusesV4Downgrade|Driven, passes|\n91||3|Closed trust document|DecodeTrust / TestDecodeTrustRefusals|Driven, passes|\n92||4|Missing/corrupt trust refuses|ReadSnapshot / TestReadSnapshotMissingStore, TestCorruptTrustRefusedNeverEmpty|Driven, passes|\n93||5|Fresh issuance|IssueCredential / TestIssueCredentialProfile|Driven, passes|\n94||6|Exact profile and time bounds|VerifyProfile / TestVerifyProfileRefusals, TestVerifyProfileRefusesJustPastExpiry|Driven, passes|\n95||7|Explicit tuple enrollment|Store.Enroll / TestEnrollRefusals|Driven, passes; OOB human verification remains operator act|\n96||8|Mapping uniqueness|DecodeTrust / TestDecodeTrustRefusals duplicate-root/key rows|Driven, passes|\n97||9|Rotation/retirement bounds|Rotate, MarkRetiring / TestRotateBoundedWindow, TestMarkRetiringCapsAtLeafExpiry|Driven, passes|\n98||10|Revocation tombstones|Revoke, Enroll / TestRevokeTombstone, TestRevokedLeafNeverReenrolls|Driven, passes serially|\n99||11|Old-generation mutation refusal|WithMutationAuthorization / TestReviewerStaleMutation|Driven, FAIL|\n100||12|Boundary/revoke serialization|WithMutationAuthorization, Revoke / TestReviewerRevocationDuringBoundary|Driven, FAIL|\n101||13|Coherent config plus trust snapshot|ReadSnapshot returns trust only; caller supplies allowlist|Not established; missing combined production proof|\n102||14|Unix owner custody|Open, ValidateCustody / TestCustodyRefusals, TestValidateCustodyBindsDirectory|Driven on Darwin, passes|\n103||15|Windows equivalent ACLs|verifyOwner|Not driven; implementation gap F4|\n104||16|Complete peers and selected credential|PreviewV4 / TestPreviewV4PeerEnrollment, TestPreviewV4CredentialGates|Driven, passes|\n105||17|Exact preview and confirmation|ApplyV4 / TestApplyV4PreviewMismatch, TestApplyV4ConfirmRequiredWithDrops|Driven, passes serially|\n106||18|Current source/generation apply|ApplyV4 / TestApplyV4StaleSource, TestApplyV4StaleGeneration|Driven, passes serially; transaction window remains|\n107||19|Crash-durable config/trust pair|applyV4, Load, ReadSnapshot / TestReviewerCrashBetweenConfigAndGeneration|Driven, FAIL|\n108||20|Explicit backup rollback|RollbackV4 / TestRollbackV4, TestRollbackV4BackupGates|Driven, passes normal/error paths; stopping channels belongs to RPC/operator boundary|\n109||21|Secret exclusion across export surfaces|ExcludedFromReplication, local walk only|Not production-driven across required surfaces|\n110|\n111|Live TLS/handshake/dispatch admission and one-second stream closure remain the\n112|RPC task's scope, not a newly invented guarantee of this leaf. Peer distribution\n113|is operator duty. No blanket waiver for custody, generation or crash atomicity.\n114|\n115|## Verification and provenance\n116|\n117|- Reviewed supplied producer results, retry2, retry3, refresh and CR validation.\n118|- Independently verified base includes adoption trunk 8cf4aaa; base signature\n119|  verifies as oparin@me.com. Candidate archive contains the v0.6.0 adoption.\n120|- Patch SHA256 matches a1ee1e7dd2120ce8bb883d55ad3092bd53c46432e7791ddc2c8bf30334266d81.\n121|- RPC backups 15/15 and parked untracked files 11/11 match manifest hashes;\n122|  none of those paths overlaps the 44-path CR. RPC preservation resource remains\n123|  attached to TASK-260830-z1yxg9. No checkpointed SSH/peer changes were modified.\n124|- Reran immutable config/hosttrust/peeridentity package tests with -count=1\n125|  -cover: exit 0; coverage 93.2%, 77.0%, 97.5%. Initial live-tree run also exit 0;\n126|  acceptance conclusions use the immutable archive run. An intermediate masked\n127|  run passed but is superseded by the complete three-package rerun.\n128|- Accepted whole-repository build/vet/full-suite and publication validation from\n129|  the attached rev3 log rather than rerunning unrelated gates. Those green\n130|  checks do not override the three new negative failures.\n131|- Reran four semantic narrowing overlays: stale-direction, custody-0644,\n132|  preview-length, confirm-drops, each exit 1 with the expected named failing\n133|  test. Two neutral controls pass exit 0. Harnesses exit 0. Probe sources were\n134|  moved out of package test discovery before these control/mutant runs.\n135|- Independently checked producer mutation source SHA256 manifests against the\n136|  immutable archive: 25 hosttrust files and 7 config files match. Retained\n137|  producer results record 15 hosttrust kills, 3 config semantic kills plus\n138|  1 label kill, and two passing controls. This is not every-gate coverage.\n139|- New probes fail exit 1 (hosttrust two tests; config crash test). Child crash\n140|  exit 77 is asserted by its parent. Evidence archive preserves source, logs,\n141|  commands/exit accounting, mutation outputs and provenance verification script.\n142|- Readiness: Go 1.25.5 darwin/arm64, git 2.50.1, Python 3; task-board mutation\n143|  succeeded. Managed worktree lacks local skill adapters; required Curator Go\n144|  skill