{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c4c3","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a08946-5fbe-7830-b2e8-af2616179f48"},"sequence":188,"recorded_at":1780531400000371,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"b6e8a9ed-35e9-4191-9a50-1dfe1ff8a38f","payload_type":"tool.result","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"tool_result","command_id":"b6e8a9ed-35e9-4191-9a50-1dfe1ff8a38f","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"b6e8a9ed-35e9-4191-9a50-1dfe1ff8a38f"},"call_id":"call_01a08946b20579e19ec647c99140ddd5","text":"Read text file `/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.temp/resources/TASK-260909-2ez769/TASK-260909-2ez769_results.md`.\n1|# TASK-260909-2ez769 results — Host Trust Store 1.0.0 + Config 4.0.0 migration\n2|\n3|Producer: developer run RUN-260910-cc2077, 2026-09-10. Worktree left UNCOMMITTED\n4|on task-board/story/STORY-260830-1kiyj6 for handoff snapshot (no producer commit).\n5|\n6|## Resume precondition (verified, not assumed)\n7|\n8|- STORY-260908-18woqo landed on origin/main: 5d98b08 + d727513, both\n9|  `git verify-commit` Good (oparin@me.com). v0.6.0 lock on main pins\n10|  spec commit 0cbdf100dbf84df50c64f792b1f940e3a67859a6, Configuration\n11|  1.0.0-4.0.0. Normative text consumed read-only from\n12|  origin/main:internal/specdoc/SPEC.v0.6.0.md (sections 6.6, 11.10.2-11.10.5).\n13|\n14|## Foreign RPC delta (preserved, verified, parked)\n15|\n16|- All 15 enumerated bytes verified ALL-MATCH against\n17|  .temp/TASK-260830-z1yxg9/preserved-before-credentials-260910/manifest.json\n18|  before any change; tracked.patch proven byte-identical to `git diff`;\n19|  files/ copies verified BACKUP-ALL-MATCH; all modes 100644.\n20|- Preservation outcome attached to TASK-260830-z1yxg9\n21|  (TASK-260830-z1yxg9_preservation-before-credentials-260910.md) BEFORE\n22|  separation, with restoration instructions.\n23|- Parked ONLY the enumerated delta: 4 tracked paths restored to checkpoint\n24|  blobs (worktree-blob == checkpoint-blob verified per path), 11 untracked\n25|  files moved to .temp/TASK-260909-2ez769/parked-rpc-delta-260910/ (bytes\n26|  re-verified against manifest). Worktree was CLEAN after parking.\n27|- RPC task left pending/blocked; nothing from the delta was consumed.\n28|\n29|## Base transition (attempted, refused, recorded)\n30|\n31|- `task-board worktree refresh-candidate TASK-260909-2ez769` refused:\n32|  \"candidate refresh requires the final unresolved leaf\". Exact refusal kept.\n33|- No manual rebase/merge/switch performed (Story workspace forbids it).\n34|- Implementation therefore sits on checkpoint base c1eff01 (v0.5.0 pin +\n35|  checkpointed SSH/peer-identity leaves) while citing v0.6.0 normatively.\n36|  Adoption files (specpin v0.6.0, SPEC.v0.6.0.md, catalogue, cigate) were\n37|  deliberately NOT duplicated; integration must land this onto the adoption\n38|  base. New code references v0.6.0 by value, not by the adopted pin.\n39|\n40|## What was built\n41|\n42|- internal/hosttrust (new): TrustStore 1.0.0 closed reader/writer\n43|  (exact keys, duplicate-JSON-key audit, uint53 generation, sorted entries,\n44|  canonical DER, retire_at exactly-for-retiring); Profile-1 issuance\n45|  (fresh P-256 keys, exact CN/SAN/KU/EKU/BC/SKI/AKI/serials/validity,\n46|  root key destroyed) and verification (inclusive validity, no skew/grace);\n47|  owner-only custody (0700/0600, owner, no symlinks, verify-never-repair,\n48|  flock SH/EX lock); atomic crash-durable commits (stage+fsync+rename+dirsync,\n49|  staging ignored, corrupt never empty); explicit enrollment with OOB tuple\n50|  reproduction; fresh-key bounded rotation (24h cap, leaf-expiry cap, no\n51|  second rotation, MarkRetiring for peer catch-up); revocation tombstones\n52|  with generation bump; current-generation dispatch/mutation authorization\n53|  (binding check, exact leaf/root/SPKI match, allowlist, hello equality,\n54|  EX-serialized boundaries); public-only enrollment export; replication\n55|  exclusion registry; redacted renderings throughout.\n56|- internal/config: Version4/TransportSSHTLS13/HostChannelVersion constants;\n57|  closed rawV4 reader (required transport, no default; required closed\n58|  host_channel; no per-peer override; no cert bytes possible by shape);\n59|  v4 validation; EncodeVersion4 (defence-in-depth re-read); EncodeCurrent\n60|  refuses v4 values; Migrate→v4 refuses toward Preview/Apply;\n61|  Migrate v4→v3 refuses as downgrade; AssessCompatibility v4/v4 compatible,\n62|  v3-reader read-only; PreviewV4 (v3-only source, admitted credential,\n63|  complete peer enrollment or named drops, exact bytes); ApplyV4 (confirm,\n64|  source/gen/bytes/custody re-validation, backup, generation-bump commit\n65|  with config recovery); RollbackV4 (ack, backup-only, generation bump,\n66|  idempotent no-op).\n67|- interop: v4 snapshots flow through peeridentity.FromSnapshot unchanged\n68|  (internal/peeridentity/v4_interop_test.go).\n69|- census: secprim roster extended to hosttrust package + 5 disposition rows\n70|  (40 sites); redaction/error-identity discipline preserved.\n71|\n72|## AC coverage: 21 of 21 rows driven through production entry points\n73|\n74|Reader: config.Decode (schema_v4 tests), hosttrust.DecodeTrust (trust tests).\n75|Refusals missing/partial/unreadable/ambiguous/downgraded: store + preview +\n76|apply + rollback absent/corrupt/dup/legacy cases. No legacy fallback:\n77|required transport, Migrate-v4-explicit, EncodeCurrent-v4 refusal, v3-reader\n78|read-only. Enrollment/mapping/rotation/revocation/generation-auth: lifecycle\n79|+ authorize tests. Owner-only atomic crash-durable writes: custody tests incl.\n80|fault-seam commit failure, staging discipline, trust-commit recovery.\n81|Exact-preview migration + peer enrollment + durable apply/rollback: preview,\n82|apply, rollback tests. Preservation: full existing suites green unmodified +\n83|interop test. Platform/crash evidence: darwin 0700/0600/owner/symlink/fault\n84|tests (this run). No secret replication: exclusion registry + walk test +\n85|census rows + redaction tests.\n86|Stated bounds (not production-driven here): live TLS 1.3 launch/handshake/\n87|hello/dispatch and stream close-down belong to the RPC transport task\n88|(sections 11.10.1/11.10.4 transport gates); Windows DACL beyond owner-SID\n89|equality has no runner here (code builds for windows, unix fully enforced);\n90|peer-side distribution of enrollment/rotation/revocation is operator duty per\n91|spec; server-flag refusals (no-host-channel) have no call site in this base.\n92|\n93|## Negative + mutation evidence (truthful counts)\n94|\n95|- hosttrust/mutations.py: 11 narrowing mutants killed by named tests, 1\n96|  neutral SURVIVED control. config/mutations_v4.py: 3 narrowing + 1\n97|  label-precision mutant killed, 1 neutral SURVIVED control.\n98|- No gate searches source text for a token (all gates operate on decoded\n99|  values/DER/parsed TOML), so the preserve-token behavioral-mutant clause is\n100|  vacuous; stated here, not silently skipped.\n101|- Evidence preserved: .temp/TASK-260909-2ez769/mutations-hosttrust/ and\n102|  mutations-config/ (results.json, table.md, manifest.json with source\n103|  digests and per-mutant exit/test lists).\n104|- Gates: go build ./... ok; go vet ./... clean; gofmt clean;\n105|  go test ./... -count=1 all ok; go test ./... -cover all ok\n106|  (hosttrust 76.5%, config 93.2%; remainder is fault-branch/error-path\n107|  plumbing and Windows-only files); 245 top-level tests pass across the four\n108|  touched packages; config refusal-inventory audit passes (3 justified\n109|  defence-in-depth subsumptions pinned in-file); secprim census passes.\n110|\n111|## Notes for reviewer/integrator\n112|\n113|- MarkRetiring was added during testing: peer rotation catch-up had no local\n114|  path (only self-rotation existed). It bounds a peer entry with the same\n115|  24h/enrolled_at rules.\n116|- ensureOwnerDir verifies existing directories and never repairs them:\n117|  silently narrowing a widened directory would mask the violation (found by\n118|  TestCustodyRefusals).\n119|- Secret-census blind spot (honest): LeafKeyDER and \"private-key.pem\" evade\n120|  the token list (\"key\" alone is not a token; hyphen vs underscore). Not\n121|  widening the token list here (would re-derive the whole repo); covered by\n122|  TestNoSecretReplication + redaction tests instead.\n123|- Untracked candidates for review: internal/hosttrust/*,\n124|  internal/config/migration_v4*.go + schema_v4_test.go +\n125|  migration_v4_test.go + migration_v4_apply_test.go + mutations_v4.py,\n126|  internal/peeridentity/v4_interop_test.go. Tracked edits: config migration/\n127|  schema/validation/writer, refusal pin, secprim census rows.","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"read_file","outcome":"success"}}}
