{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c835","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a08946-5fbe-7830-b2e8-af2616179f48"},"sequence":629,"recorded_at":1780531400001253,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"b6e8a9ed-35e9-4191-9a50-1dfe1ff8a38f","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"b6e8a9ed-35e9-4191-9a50-1dfe1ff8a38f","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"b6e8a9ed-35e9-4191-9a50-1dfe1ff8a38f"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a08947-5fd8-7fe0-a79d-3891179692dc"},"task_id":"01a08947-5fd8-7fe0-a79d-3891179692dc","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a08947-5fd8-7fe0-a79d-3891179692dc","chunk":"Read text file `internal/specdoc/SPEC.v0.6.0.md`.\n(8097 line(s) above)\n8098|#### 11.10.2 Certificate issuance and enrolled trust\n8099|\n8100|Host Credential Profile 1 is part of Host Channel 1, with no online CA service.\n8101|For each credential generation the host generates two distinct CSPRNG ECDSA\n8102|P-256 key pairs locally: a self-signed root CA and a leaf signed by that CA.\n8103|Root and leaf use X.509 v3, ECDSA-with-SHA256 signatures and distinct positive\n8104|random 128-bit serial numbers. The root is used only to sign this one leaf;\n8105|its private key MUST be destroyed after successful issuance. Rotation generates\n8106|both fresh keys and certificates. Reissuing a leaf under an enrolled CA does\n8107|not enroll it. TLS sends only the leaf; the exact root is already local trust.\n8108|\n8109|| Certificate member | Root | Leaf |\n8110|| --- | --- | --- |\n8111|| Subject / issuer | CN <code>AX Host Root HOST_UUID</code>, self-issued | CN <code>AX Host HOST_UUID</code>, issuer equals root subject |\n8112|| Basic Constraints (critical) | CA=true, pathLen=0 | CA=false, no pathLen |\n8113|| Key Usage (critical) | keyCertSign only | digitalSignature only |\n8114|| Extended Key Usage (noncritical) | Absent | Exactly clientAuth and serverAuth |\n8115|| Subject Alternative Name (noncritical) | Absent | Exactly one DNS name <code>HOST_UUID.host.ax.invalid</code>; no other SAN type |\n8116|| Validity | notBefore=issuance time minus 300s; notAfter=notBefore plus 366 days | Same notBefore; notAfter=notBefore plus 90 days |\n8117|| Subject Key Identifier (noncritical) | SHA-1 of subjectPublicKey BIT STRING contents | Same construction for leaf key |\n8118|| Authority Key Identifier (noncritical) | Root SKI | Root SKI |\n8119|\n8120|HOST_UUID is the configured lowercase canonical UUIDv7, without braces. No\n8121|wildcard, CN-only name, alternative UUID, extra subject attribute, extension,\n8122|intermediate, AIA fetch, CRL URL or OCSP dependency is allowed in this profile.\n8123|The DNS SAN is a verification name, never a DNS lookup or network endpoint.\n8124|Root self-signature, leaf signature, exact fields above, valid P-256 public\n8125|points, root/leaf lifetime and current validity of both certificates MUST be\n8126|checked at enrollment and handshake. Certificate validity uses the actual\n8127|local UTC time inclusively within notBefore/notAfter; no extra acceptance skew\n8128|or expiry grace is allowed. Unavailable/untrusted local time refuses admission;\n8129|clock correction cannot extend a previously scheduled stream expiry. No FIPS\n8130|certification or hardware non-exportability is claimed by choosing P-256.\n8131|\n8132|Host Trust Store 1.0.0 is owner-only JSON at\n8133|<code>STATE_DIR/host-channel/trust.json</code>. It is machine-local authority,\n8134|not an immutable mesh object, and has exactly these fields:\n8135|\n8136|| Field | Type / constraint |\n8137|| --- | --- |\n8138|| <code>schema</code> | Exact <code>urn:ax:schema:host-trust-store</code> |\n8139|| <code>schema_version</code> | Exact <code>1.0.0</code> |\n8140|| <code>generation</code> | uint53 greater than zero; increments by one per committed trust/config authorization change; exhaustion refuses mutation |\n8141|| <code>entries</code> | CredentialEntry[0..4096], sorted by credential_id, no duplicates |\n8142|\n8143|Each CredentialEntry contains exactly <code>host_id:UUIDv7</code>,\n8144|<code>credential_id:digest</code> (SHA-256 of leaf DER),\n8145|<code>spki_id:digest</code> (SHA-256 of leaf SubjectPublicKeyInfo DER),\n8146|<code>root_id:digest</code> (SHA-256 of root DER),\n8147|<code>leaf_der:base64url</code>, <code>root_der:base64url</code> (each unpadded,\n8148|canonical and decoding to 1..16384 bytes),\n8149|<code>state:active|retiring|revoked</code>, <code>enrolled_at:timestamp</code>,\n8150|and <code>retire_at:timestamp|null</code>. The last field is non-null exactly\n8151|for retiring entries and later than enrolled_at. Revoked entries retain their\n8152|public bytes permanently as reuse tombstones. An unreadable, malformed,\n8153|partially read, duplicate-key, unknown-field or missing store is never an empty\n8154|store. Initial creation of an empty generation-1 store is explicit local setup.\n8155|\n8156|Enrollment is local operator authorization of the tuple (host UUID, leaf DER\n8157|fingerprint, SPKI fingerprint, root DER fingerprint), verified over an\n8158|independent authenticated out-of-band channel. Imported public bytes MUST\n8159|reproduce those fingerprints and the profile before the transaction commits.\n8160|SSH discovery, a first hello, a remote claim, and a certificate being self-signed\n8161|are not approval. Remote RPC cannot mutate the trust store. Both directions\n8162|need enrollment; one side enrolling another does not imply reciprocity.\n8163|\n8164|Across all entries, including revoked ones, a leaf, leaf public key or root\n8165|MUST NOT map to more than one host UUID. Multiple entries for the same leaf or\n8166|SPKI are invalid, including attempted renewal with the same key. Duplicate\n8167|root IDs are also invalid, even for the same UUID. At most two\n8168|non-revoked credentials may belong to a host, solely during rotation. A root\n8169|trusted for one host never grants its other issued certificates admission.\n8170|After ordinary TLS verification, an exact leaf/root/SPKI match against one\n8171|currently admitted entry yields the verified UUID. Zero or multiple matches\n8172|refuse. SAN alone and CA membership alone are insufficient. Both EKUs are\n8173|required by the profile; chain verification additionally validates serverAuth\n8174|at the client and clientAuth at the server.\n8175|\n8176|Local leaf PEM and PKCS#8 private-key PEM are stored under\n8177|<code>STATE_DIR/host-channel/credentials/HEX_CREDENTIAL_ID/</code> as\n8178|<code>certificate.pem</code> and <code>private-key.pem</code>; HEX_CREDENTIAL_ID\n8179|is the 64 lowercase hex characters after <code>sha256:</code>. The root public\n8180|PEM is <code>root.pem</code>. No other file may select identity. Validate the\n8181|private/public match, profile and configured host ID before use. Directories\n8182|are 0700 and files 0600 on Unix; Windows requires equivalent owner-only ACLs.\n8183|Reject symlinks/reparse escapes or group/world write access. Do not forward SSH\n8184|agents or reuse SSH/provider keys. Credential/trust files, backups, private\n8185|keys and authorization caches MUST NOT enter replication, snapshots, cloning,\n8186|Session Directory, logs or exported diagnostic bundles. Operators exchange only\n8187|explicitly selected public enrollment material outside replication.\n8188|\n8189|#### 11.10.3 Rotation, revocation and authorization generations\n8190|\n8191|Rotation keeps host UUID and creates a new credential. Explicitly enroll the\n8192|new tuple on each participating peer before selecting it in Config-4. The\n8193|local atomic trust transition admits the new entry as active and marks the old\n8194|entry retiring with a fixed retire_at no more than 24 hours after that\n8195|transition and no later than old leaf expiry. There is no overlap extension;\n8196|no second rotation starts until the retiring entry is revoked. Failed or\n8197|incomplete enrollment leaves the new route unavailable, never auto-trusted.\n8198|At retire_at old admission ends and old streams close even if the new route\n8199|is unavailable. A peer offline during rotation must explicitly catch up; no\n8200|mesh-wide atomic enrollment or central CA availability is assumed.\n8201|\n8202|Trust changes and Config-4 peer/credential changes share a machine-local\n8203|cross-process authorization lock and crash-durable generation transaction.\n8204|Readers MUST obtain one coherent committed snapshot (config plus trust), never\n8205|mix an old allowlist with new credentials. Every opened stream binds the local\n8206|credential ID, verified remote credential ID/UUID and snapshot generation.\n8207|A trust/config commit invalidates all streams of the prior generation; every\n8208|process, including daemonless RPC children, MUST close them within one second\n8209|of the commit using cancellation plus a bounded watchdog, even when idle.\n8210|Missing/failed generation reads close the stream. Filesystem notifications\n8211|alone are insufficient. At certificate expiry or retire_at the same rule\n8212|applies, with no new dispatch at or after the deadline. Process crashes close\n8213|the underlying stream; a dead process is not an authorization subscriber.\n8214|\n8215|Every application dispatch checks current generation, credential validity,\n8216|allowlist membership and authenticated hello. Its check and dispatch admission\n8217|MUST hold the same authorization lock, so revocation cannot commit between them.\n8218|A read admitted before revocation may be interrupted by stream cancellation;\n8219|no new read is admitted afterward from the stale generation. Each mutation, including resumed\n8220|transfer, retry, queued work and recovery, additionally rechecks these facts\n8221|under the authorization lock immediately before each externally visible\n8222|side-effect boundary. The generation check and that boundary serialize with\n8223|revocation/config commit. Work prepared under an old generation cannot gain\n8224|new authority by refreshing a cached number: discard its authorization and\n8225|replan/revalidate through a fresh mutually authenticated connection. Existing\n8226|lease, operation and idempotency checks still apply. An effect already committed\n8227|before revocation is not undone; pending work must stop at the next boundary\n(more lines below)","final_result":true}}}
{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c837","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a08946-5fbe-7830-b2e8-af2616179f48"},"sequence":630,"recorded_at":1780531400001255,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"b6e8a9ed-35e9-4191-9a50-1dfe1ff8a38f","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.completed","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"b6e8a9ed-35e9-4191-9a50-1dfe1ff8a38f","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"b6e8a9ed-35e9-4191-9a50-1dfe1ff8a38f"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a08947-5fd8-7fe0-a79d-3891179692dc"},"task_id":"01a08947-5fd8-7fe0-a79d-3891179692dc","event":{"kind":"completed","task_id":"01a08947-5fd8-7fe0-a79d-3891179692dc"}}}
{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c839","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a08946-5fbe-7830-b2e8-af2616179f48"},"sequence":631,"recorded_at":1780531400001257,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"b6e8a9ed-35e9-4191-9a50-1dfe1ff8a38f","payload_type":"tool.result","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"tool_result","command_id":"b6e8a9ed-35e9-4191-9a50-1dfe1ff8a38f","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"b6e8a9ed-35e9-4191-9a50-1dfe1ff8a38f"},"call_id":"call_01a089475c277cc380e4db9e3c4e9cfb","text":"Read text file `internal/specdoc/SPEC.v0.6.0.md`.\n(8097 line(s) above)\n8098|#### 11.10.2 Certificate issuance and enrolled trust\n8099|\n8100|Host Credential Profile 1 is part of Host Channel 1, with no online CA service.\n8101|For each credential generation the host generates two distinct CSPRNG ECDSA\n8102|P-256 key pairs locally: a self-signed root CA and a leaf signed by that CA.\n8103|Root and leaf use X.509 v3, ECDSA-with-SHA256 signatures and distinct positive\n8104|random 128-bit serial numbers. The root is used only to sign this one leaf;\n8105|its private key MUST be destroyed after successful issuance. Rotation generates\n8106|both fresh keys and certificates. Reissuing a leaf under an enrolled CA does\n8107|not enroll it. TLS sends only the leaf; the exact root is already local trust.\n8108|\n8109|| Certificate member | Root | Leaf |\n8110|| --- | --- | --- |\n8111|| Subject / issuer | CN <code>AX Host Root HOST_UUID</code>, self-issued | CN <code>AX Host HOST_UUID</code>, issuer equals root subject |\n8112|| Basic Constraints (critical) | CA=true, pathLen=0 | CA=false, no pathLen |\n8113|| Key Usage (critical) | keyCertSign only | digitalSignature only |\n8114|| Extended Key Usage (noncritical) | Absent | Exactly clientAuth and serverAuth |\n8115|| Subject Alternative Name (noncritical) | Absent | Exactly one DNS name <code>HOST_UUID.host.ax.invalid</code>; no other SAN type |\n8116|| Validity | notBefore=issuance time minus 300s; notAfter=notBefore plus 366 days | Same notBefore; notAfter=notBefore plus 90 days |\n8117|| Subject Key Identifier (noncritical) | SHA-1 of subjectPublicKey BIT STRING contents | Same construction for leaf key |\n8118|| Authority Key Identifier (noncritical) | Root SKI | Root SKI |\n8119|\n8120|HOST_UUID is the configured lowercase canonical UUIDv7, without braces. No\n8121|wildcard, CN-only name, alternative UUID, extra subject attribute, extension,\n8122|intermediate, AIA fetch, CRL URL or OCSP dependency is allowed in this profile.\n8123|The DNS SAN is a verification name, never a DNS lookup or network endpoint.\n8124|Root self-signature, leaf signature, exact fields above, valid P-256 public\n8125|points, root/leaf lifetime and current validity of both certificates MUST be\n8126|checked at enrollment and handshake. Certificate validity uses the actual\n8127|local UTC time inclusively within notBefore/notAfter; no extra acceptance skew\n8128|or expiry grace is allowed. Unavailable/untrusted local time refuses admission;\n8129|clock correction cannot extend a previously scheduled stream expiry. No FIPS\n8130|certification or hardware non-exportability is claimed by choosing P-256.\n8131|\n8132|Host Trust Store 1.0.0 is owner-only JSON at\n8133|<code>STATE_DIR/host-channel/trust.json</code>. It is machine-local authority,\n8134|not an immutable mesh object, and has exactly these fields:\n8135|\n8136|| Field | Type / constraint |\n8137|| --- | --- |\n8138|| <code>schema</code> | Exact <code>urn:ax:schema:host-trust-store</code> |\n8139|| <code>schema_version</code> | Exact <code>1.0.0</code> |\n8140|| <code>generation</code> | uint53 greater than zero; increments by one per committed trust/config authorization change; exhaustion refuses mutation |\n8141|| <code>entries</code> | CredentialEntry[0..4096], sorted by credential_id, no duplicates |\n8142|\n8143|Each CredentialEntry contains exactly <code>host_id:UUIDv7</code>,\n8144|<code>credential_id:digest</code> (SHA-256 of leaf DER),\n8145|<code>spki_id:digest</code> (SHA-256 of leaf SubjectPublicKeyInfo DER),\n8146|<code>root_id:digest</code> (SHA-256 of root DER),\n8147|<code>leaf_der:base64url</code>, <code>root_der:base64url</code> (each unpadded,\n8148|canonical and decoding to 1..16384 bytes),\n8149|<code>state:active|retiring|revoked</code>, <code>enrolled_at:timestamp</code>,\n8150|and <code>retire_at:timestamp|null</code>. The last field is non-null exactly\n8151|for retiring entries and later than enrolled_at. Revoked entries retain their\n8152|public bytes permanently as reuse tombstones. An unreadable, malformed,\n8153|partially read, duplicate-key, unknown-field or missing store is never an empty\n8154|store. Initial creation of an empty generation-1 store is explicit local setup.\n8155|\n8156|Enrollment is local operator authorization of the tuple (host UUID, leaf DER\n8157|fingerprint, SPKI fingerprint, root DER fingerprint), verified over an\n8158|independent authenticated out-of-band channel. Imported public bytes MUST\n8159|reproduce those fingerprints and the profile before the transaction commits.\n8160|SSH discovery, a first hello, a remote claim, and a certificate being self-signed\n8161|are not approval. Remote RPC cannot mutate the trust store. Both directions\n8162|need enrollment; one side enrolling another does not imply reciprocity.\n8163|\n8164|Across all entries, including revoked ones, a leaf, leaf public key or root\n8165|MUST NOT map to more than one host UUID. Multiple entries for the same leaf or\n8166|SPKI are invalid, including attempted renewal with the same key. Duplicate\n8167|root IDs are also invalid, even for the same UUID. At most two\n8168|non-revoked credentials may belong to a host, solely during rotation. A root\n8169|trusted for one host never grants its other issued certificates admission.\n8170|After ordinary TLS verification, an exact leaf/root/SPKI match against one\n8171|currently admitted entry yields the verified UUID. Zero or multiple matches\n8172|refuse. SAN alone and CA membership alone are insufficient. Both EKUs are\n8173|required by the profile; chain verification additionally validates serverAuth\n8174|at the client and clientAuth at the server.\n8175|\n8176|Local leaf PEM and PKCS#8 private-key PEM are stored under\n8177|<code>STATE_DIR/host-channel/credentials/HEX_CREDENTIAL_ID/</code> as\n8178|<code>certificate.pem</code> and <code>private-key.pem</code>; HEX_CREDENTIAL_ID\n8179|is the 64 lowercase hex characters after <code>sha256:</code>. The root public\n8180|PEM is <code>root.pem</code>. No other file may select identity. Validate the\n8181|private/public match, profile and configured host ID before use. Directories\n8182|are 0700 and files 0600 on Unix; Windows requires equivalent owner-only ACLs.\n8183|Reject symlinks/reparse escapes or group/world write access. Do not forward SSH\n8184|agents or reuse SSH/provider keys. Credential/trust files, backups, private\n8185|keys and authorization caches MUST NOT enter replication, snapshots, cloning,\n8186|Session Directory, logs or exported diagnostic bundles. Operators exchange only\n8187|explicitly selected public enrollment material outside replication.\n8188|\n8189|#### 11.10.3 Rotation, revocation and authorization generations\n8190|\n8191|Rotation keeps host UUID and creates a new credential. Explicitly enroll the\n8192|new tuple on each participating peer before selecting it in Config-4. The\n8193|local atomic trust transition admits the new entry as active and marks the old\n8194|entry retiring with a fixed retire_at no more than 24 hours after that\n8195|transition and no later than old leaf expiry. There is no overlap extension;\n8196|no second rotation starts until the retiring entry is revoked. Failed or\n8197|incomplete enrollment leaves the new route unavailable, never auto-trusted.\n8198|At retire_at old admission ends and old streams close even if the new route\n8199|is unavailable. A peer offline during rotation must explicitly catch up; no\n8200|mesh-wide atomic enrollment or central CA availability is assumed.\n8201|\n8202|Trust changes and Config-4 peer/credential changes share a machine-local\n8203|cross-process authorization lock and crash-durable generation transaction.\n8204|Readers MUST obtain one coherent committed snapshot (config plus trust), never\n8205|mix an old allowlist with new credentials. Every opened stream binds the local\n8206|credential ID, verified remote credential ID/UUID and snapshot generation.\n8207|A trust/config commit invalidates all streams of the prior generation; every\n8208|process, including daemonless RPC children, MUST close them within one second\n8209|of the commit using cancellation plus a bounded watchdog, even when idle.\n8210|Missing/failed generation reads close the stream. Filesystem notifications\n8211|alone are insufficient. At certificate expiry or retire_at the same rule\n8212|applies, with no new dispatch at or after the deadline. Process crashes close\n8213|the underlying stream; a dead process is not an authorization subscriber.\n8214|\n8215|Every application dispatch checks current generation, credential validity,\n8216|allowlist membership and authenticated hello. Its check and dispatch admission\n8217|MUST hold the same authorization lock, so revocation cannot commit between them.\n8218|A read admitted before revocation may be interrupted by stream cancellation;\n8219|no new read is admitted afterward from the stale generation. Each mutation, including resumed\n8220|transfer, retry, queued work and recovery, additionally rechecks these facts\n8221|under the authorization lock immediately before each externally visible\n8222|side-effect boundary. The generation check and that boundary serialize with\n8223|revocation/config commit. Work prepared under an old generation cannot gain\n8224|new authority by refreshing a cached number: discard its authorization and\n8225|replan/revalidate through a fresh mutually authenticated connection. Existing\n8226|lease, operation and idempotency checks still apply. An effect already committed\n8227|before revocation is not undone; pending work must stop at the next boundary\n(more lines below)","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"read_file","outcome":"success"}}}
