{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c877","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a08946-5fbe-7830-b2e8-af2616179f48"},"sequence":662,"recorded_at":1780531400001319,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"b6e8a9ed-35e9-4191-9a50-1dfe1ff8a38f","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"b6e8a9ed-35e9-4191-9a50-1dfe1ff8a38f","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"b6e8a9ed-35e9-4191-9a50-1dfe1ff8a38f"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a08947-699c-7f61-adfc-f76d6c8b2944"},"task_id":"01a08947-699c-7f61-adfc-f76d6c8b2944","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a08947-699c-7f61-adfc-f76d6c8b2944","chunk":"Read text file `internal/specdoc/SPEC.v0.6.0.md`.\n(8226 line(s) above)\n8227|before revocation is not undone; pending work must stop at the next boundary\n8228|and use the existing recovery journal. Long provider calls must not hold the\n8229|authorization lock across unbounded work; revocation cannot report success\n8230|while an effect boundary still holds prior authorization.\n8231|\n8232|Revocation is an explicit local atomic transition to revoked, increments the\n8233|generation, forbids all future admissions of that key and closes old streams.\n8234|Removing an allowlisted host also increments generation and invalidates streams.\n8235|Success means the durable decision committed; the documented one-second close\n8236|bound does not permit any later dispatch or mutation from the stale generation.\n8237|A crash after commit but before acknowledgements cannot restore authority.\n8238|Failed commits report failure; they cannot be reported as absence or success.\n8239|Revocation is local: the operator must distribute it explicitly to every peer;\n8240|a disconnected peer with stale trust cannot be claimed globally revoked.\n8241|Loss/copy/compromise of a key requires revocation and new out-of-band enrollment,\n8242|not same-key recovery. Host UUID reuse after total trust-state loss requires\n8243|operator reconciliation of every peer, never automatic enrollment.\n8244|\n8245|#### 11.10.4 Assurance and executable fixture bounds\n8246|\n8247|TLS proves possession of an enrolled private key and protects records. It does\n8248|not prove unique physical hardware, current ownership of a Session, or an\n8249|uncompromised operator/account. A copied key authenticates until each verifier\n8250|revokes it. An attacker able to read/replace local AX state, credentials or\n8251|binaries is outside this assurance. Arbitrary shell access to that account\n8252|cannot be made safe by a wrapper. A restricted server-enforced SSH account is\n8253|an alternative deployment hardening measure, not equivalent host evidence and\n8254|not a substitute for this profile. Remote attach/log CLI paths remain their\n8255|existing SSH contracts; they do not acquire RPC-5 host-channel assurance.\n8256|\n8257|The following closed gate registry defines source-level fixture families.\n8258|Each family MUST have positive and negative vectors. These are contract model\n8259|checks, not an executed TLS deployment, private-key custody proof or product\n8260|conformance result. Real certificate-chain, handshake, race/timeout and platform\n8261|acceptance remains required by <code>AC-HOST-001</code>.\n8262|\n8263|| Gate | Predicate required for admission |\n8264|| --- | --- |\n8265|| HC-TLS | Both peers verify full TLS 1.3 and exact ALPN; no resumption or early data |\n8266|| HC-CERT | Standard chain, profile, time and role verification succeed in both directions |\n8267|| HC-MAP | Exact enrolled leaf/root/key maps uniquely to the configured UUID |\n8268|| HC-HELLO | Both hello IDs equal verified UUIDs and nonce/contract/limit validation succeeds |\n8269|| HC-DISPATCH | No application dispatch before mutual TLS and hello success |\n8270|| HC-MIGRATE | Config 4 selects the explicit Host Channel 1 launch and RPC 5 only |\n8271|| HC-LIFECYCLE | Explicit enrollment and bounded fresh-key rotation; revoked keys never reenter |\n8272|| HC-GENERATION | Dispatch and every mutation boundary use the current committed authorization generation |\n8273|| HC-EXCLUDE | Credential and trust material remains local, outside replication |\n8274|| HC-PARITY | The same TLS requirements apply over OpenSSH and native Tailscale SSH |\n8275|\n8276|#### 11.10.5 Executable admission obligations\n8277|\n8278|The following closed JSON policy is normative source for the synthetic admission\n8279|predicates. The public validator reads it from SPEC.md on every invocation;\n8280|there is no independently hard-coded admission model. Every field is required,\n8281|unknown fields refuse, and all field predicates must hold. Predicates apply to\n8282|every invocation, including request, resume, retry, queue and recovery, on both\n8283|SSH transports; client/server facts are separate required obligations. The entrypoint and\n8284|carrier facts are synthetic execution context, not new RPC wire members. A\n8285|conditional predicate cannot grant an exception to another obligation.\n8286|\n8287|Operators are closed: `eq` is type-exact JSON equality; `range` is an inclusive\n8288|integer interval (booleans excluded); `in` is type-exact set membership;\n8289|`equal_field` is type-exact equality with another present field; `singleton_field`\n8290|is exactly a one-element array of that field; `uuid7` requires the canonical\n8291|lowercase UUIDv7 grammar; `all` is conjunction. `when` has exactly `field`, `in`\n8292|and `require`: it applies its predicate only when the named fact is in the given\n8293|set. It exists to make scope changes executable and testable, not to authorize\n8294|narrowing the universal obligations in this revision. Missing or mistyped\n8295|operands, duplicate keys, unsupported operators and unreadable policy refuse.\n8296|\n(more lines below)","final_result":true}}}
