nds\n8246|\n8247|TLS proves possession of an enrolled private key and protects records. It does\n8248|not prove unique physical hardware, current ownership of a Session, or an\n8249|uncompromised operator/account. A copied key authenticates until each verifier\n8250|revokes it. An attacker able to read/replace local AX state, credentials or\n8251|binaries is outside this assurance. Arbitrary shell access to that account\n8252|cannot be made safe by a wrapper. A restricted server-enforced SSH account is\n8253|an alternative deployment hardening measure, not equivalent host evidence and\n8254|not a substitute for this profile. Remote attach/log CLI paths remain their\n8255|existing SSH contracts; they do not acquire RPC-5 host-channel assurance.\n8256|\n8257|The following closed gate registry defines source-level fixture families.\n8258|Each family MUST have positive and negative vectors. These are contract model\n8259|checks, not an executed TLS deployment, private-key custody proof or product\n8260|conformance result. Real certificate-chain, handshake, race/timeout and platform\n8261|acceptance remains required by <code>AC-HOST-001</code>.\n8262|\n8263|| Gate | Predicate required for admission |\n8264|| --- | --- |\n8265|| HC-TLS | Both peers verify full TLS 1.3 and exact ALPN; no resumption or early data |\n8266|| HC-CERT | Standard chain, profile, time and role verification succeed in both directions |\n8267|| HC-MAP | Exact enrolled leaf/root/key maps uniquely to the configured UUID |\n8268|| HC-HELLO | Both hello IDs equal verified UUIDs and nonce/contract/limit validation succeeds |\n8269|| HC-DISPATCH | No application dispatch before mutual TLS and hello success |\n8270|| HC-MIGRATE | Config 4 selects the explicit Host Channel 1 launch and RPC 5 only |\n8271|| HC-LIFECYCLE | Explicit enrollment and bounded fresh-key rotation; revoked keys never reenter |\n8272|| HC-GENERATION | Dispatch and every mutation boundary use the current committed authorization generation |\n8273|| HC-EXCLUDE | Credential and trust material remains local, outside replication |\n8274|| HC-PARITY | The same TLS requirements apply over OpenSSH and native Tailscale SSH |\n8275|\n8276|#### 11.10.5 Executable admission obligations\n8277|\n8278|The following closed JSON policy is normative source for the synthetic admission\n8279|predicates. The public validator reads it from SPEC.md on every invocation;\n8280|there is no independently hard-coded admission model. Every field is required,\n8281|unknown fields refuse, and all field predicates must hold. Predicates apply to\n8282|every invocation, including request, resume, retry, queue and recovery, on both\n8283|SSH transports; client/server facts are separate required obligations. The entrypoint and\n8284|carrier facts are synthetic execution context, not new RPC wire members. A\n8285|conditional predicate cannot grant an exception to another obligation.\n8286|\n8287|Operators are closed: `eq` is type-exact JSON equality; `range` is an inclusive\n8288|integer interval (booleans excluded); `in` is type-exact set membership;\n8289|`equal_field` is type-exact equality with another present field; `singleton_field`\n8290|is exactly a one-element array of that field; `uuid7` requires the canonical\n8291|lowercase UUIDv7 grammar; `all` is conjunction. `when` has exactly `field`, `in`\n8292|and `require`: it applies its predicate only when the named fact is in the given\n8293|set. It exists to make scope changes executable and testable, not to authorize\n8294|narrowing the universal obligations in this revision. Missing or mistyped\n8295|operands, duplicate keys, unsupported operators and unreadable policy refuse.\n8296|\n(more lines below)","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"read_file","outcome":"success"}}}
{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c87d","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a08946-5fbe-7830-b2e8-af2616179f48"},"sequence":665,"recorded_at":1780531400001325,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"b6e8a9ed-35e9-4191-9a50-1dfe1ff8a38f","payload_type":"tool.result","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"tool_result","command_id":"b6e8a9ed-35e9-4191-9a50-1dfe1ff8a38f","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"b6e8a9ed-35e9-4191-9a50-1dfe1ff8a38f"},"call_id":"call_01a0894765d07a3386e5cbd693467a98","text":"Read text file `internal/specdoc/SPEC.v0.6.0.md`.\n(2635 line(s) above)\n2636|### 6.6 Configuration 4.0.0 host-channel migration\n2637|\n2638|Configuration 4.0.0 retains Configuration 3.0.0 except for the following exact\n2639|changes. All other closed members, path precedence and five environment\n2640|variables remain unchanged. No secret or TLS-verification override is added.\n2641|\n2642|| Key | Required value / constraint |\n2643|| --- | --- |\n2644|| <code>schema_version</code> | Exact <code>4.0.0</code> |\n2645|| <code>mesh.transport</code> | Required, exact <code>ssh_tls13</code>; no default or alternative |\n2646|| <code>mesh.host_channel</code> | Required, exact closed table below |\n2647|\n2648|The <code>mesh.host_channel</code> table contains exactly:\n2649|\n2650|| Key | Required value / constraint |\n2651|| --- | --- |\n2652|| <code>version</code> | Exact <code>1.0.0</code> |\n2653|| <code>credential_id</code> | SHA-256 digest of the local leaf certificate DER |\n2654|\n2655|No per-peer override exists: every peer in a Config-4 mesh requires Host\n2656|Channel 1 and RPC 5. The credential is loaded from the machine-local Section\n2657|11.10.2 store; neither a certificate nor private-key bytes belong in TOML.\n2658|The existing endpoint/SSH authentication and host-ID allowlist remain necessary\n2659|but are insufficient without enrolled TLS identity. Unknown/missing/partial\n2660|configuration, credential or trust state is a refusal, never legacy selection.\n2661|\n2662|Migration is an explicit local operator action, never first-connect behavior.\n2663|First upgrade both binaries while keeping the old configuration bytes intact;\n2664|create local credentials and exchange public enrollment material out of band;\n2665|validate all intended peers' UUIDs and fingerprints; then preview a Config-4\n2666|replacement with the retained Config-3 fields, selected credential and complete\n2667|peer set. Apply only after explicit operator confirmation, an owner-only backup,\n2668|and validation of that exact preview against the current configuration/trust\n2669|generation. Older Config-1/2 inputs first use the existing explicit migrations.\n2670|A missing peer enrollment blocks activation; an operator may explicitly remove\n2671|a peer from the preview, but the implementation cannot silently drop it.\n2672|\n2673|Replacement is atomic and crash durable. On restart select only the last fully\n2674|committed configuration plus valid local trust state; partial writes park with\n2675|<code>invalid_config</code>. Config-4 readers MUST NOT rewrite historical files,\n2676|and old readers MUST refuse Config-4 mutation. A Config-4 installation refuses\n2677|the unflagged legacy server invocation before reading stdin. A Config-1/2/3\n2678|installation refuses the flagged host-channel invocation. No byte sniffing,\n2679|extension field, argv host UUID, environment value, or failed handshake can\n2680|select a fallback. Legacy RPC 2/3/4 dual-stack obligations apply only to explicitly\n2681|legacy installations; they never require a Config-4 endpoint to accept legacy.\n2682|An operator rollback requires stopping every host channel, explicit replacement\n2683|of configuration from the preserved backup, and acknowledgement that the legacy\n2684|installation has no Host Channel assurance; it is not a connection retry.\n2685|\n2686|## 7. Provider plugin protocol\n2687|\n2688|### 7.1 Discovery and trust\n2689|\n2690|Built-in support covers <code>codex</code>, <code>claude</code>,\n2691|<code>gemini</code>, <code>muse</code>, <code>antigravity</code>, and\n2692|<code>pi</code>. External provider executables are named\n2693|<code>ax-provider-&lt;id&gt;</code>, where <code>id</code> matches\n2694|<code>[a-z][a-z0-9-]{0,31}</code>.\n2695|\n2696|Candidate discovery order is:\n2697|\n2698|1. configured <code>providers.plugin_dirs</code> in listed order;\n2699|2. built-in adapters; then\n2700|3. <code>PATH</code>, only when <code>allow_path_plugins</code> is true.\n(more lines below)","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"read_file","outcome":"success"}}}
