{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c8a9","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a08946-5fbe-7830-b2e8-af2616179f48"},"sequence":687,"recorded_at":1780531400001369,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"b6e8a9ed-35e9-4191-9a50-1dfe1ff8a38f","payload_type":"tool.result","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"tool_result","command_id":"b6e8a9ed-35e9-4191-9a50-1dfe1ff8a38f","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"b6e8a9ed-35e9-4191-9a50-1dfe1ff8a38f"},"call_id":"call_01a089490a557ee3822d8a338a5a4cf9","text":"{\n  \"chunk_id\": \"exec-10-1\",\n  \"command\": \"git ls-files | grep -c \\\"^\\\\.task-board\\\" ; echo \\\"===\\\"; git diff --stat HEAD -- . ':!.task-board' 2>&1 | tail -n 30; echo \\\"===LOGBOOK===\\\"; git diff HEAD -- LOGBOOK.md 2>&1 | head -n 60\",\n  \"description\": \"Check tracked board files and candidate diff\",\n  \"exit_code\": 0,\n  \"terminal_status\": \"completed\",\n  \"output\": \"2580\\n===\\n LOGBOOK.md                                       |  32 +++++++\\n internal/config/compatibility_regression_test.go |  51 +++++++---\\n internal/config/migration.go                     |  13 ++-\\n internal/config/migration_refusal_test.go        |  31 +++---\\n internal/config/migration_test.go                |  23 ++---\\n internal/config/refusal_structure_test.go        |   3 +\\n internal/config/schema.go                        |  69 ++++++++++++++\\n internal/config/schema_test.go                   |  42 +++++---\\n internal/config/validation.go                    | 116 ++++++++++++++++++++++-\\n internal/config/writer.go                        |  57 +++++++++++\\n internal/secprim/census_test.go                  |  86 ++++++++++++++++-\\n 11 files changed, 462 insertions(+), 61 deletions(-)\\n===LOGBOOK===\\ndiff --git a/LOGBOOK.md b/LOGBOOK.md\\nindex 57207fc..526bc3b 100644\\n--- a/LOGBOOK.md\\n+++ b/LOGBOOK.md\\n@@ -3,6 +3,38 @@\\n > Institutional memory. Concise, factual, high-signal.\\n > Newest entries first. One block per insight.\\n \\n+## 2026-09-10 (refresh)\\n+\\n+### TASK-260909-2ez769 refresh — story base moved c1eff01 to a89328c (trunk 8cf4aaa + v0.6.0 adoption)\\n+- REFRESH: `task-board worktree refresh-candidate` with exclusive lease (RUN-260910-a4ac2c). Round 1 (43c0e2b peer-identity): 5 file resolutions — LOGBOOK merged newest-first, README trunk + peer tail, 3 traceability files trunk-wins (v0.6.0 registry pin authoritative; v0.5.0 digest superseded). Round 2 (c1eff01 SSH): 4 resolutions reusing round-1 bytes + README with SSH `## SSH stdio transport` section appended and peer-section wording. Packet schema learned from tool errors: entries {checkpoint_oid, path, sha256, content-base64}. Both replayed commits signed oparin@me.com (41106b6, a89328c, verify-commit Good).\\n+- COMBINE: worktree restored to candidate snapshot by tool; 30 enumerated incoming paths restored from HEAD (8 adoption files incl. SPEC.v0.6.0.md, v0.6.0.lock.json, ownership.v0.6.0.json, task-board.config.json v0.6.0 cataloggen command); 6 tracked candidate files untouched by adoption kept; LOGBOOK re-merged (HEAD + 2 prior credential entries). Candidate bytes verified 40/40 match pre-refresh fingerprint.\\n+- INTEGRATION (real semantic conflicts, resolved preserving both intents): adoption tests pinned \\\"v4 reader unimplemented\\\" — now stale. `compatibility_regression_test.go` const Version4 removed (production wins, same value); v4 lanes now positive per-lane loads (windows/ax.conpty, wsl2/ax.tmux, native plugdirs); conpty-on-v4 now closed-shape refusal (ErrConfigDecode, never version refusal). `schema_test.go` v4 branch now bare-doc required-member refusal + complete-doc positive (SourceVersion 4.0.0, ssh_tls13, host_channel); \\\"unsupported major\\\" renamed. `migration_test.go` assessor now 6 read-only / 10 compatible / 0 refused (was 6/6/4). `migration_refusal_test.go` v4 row now wants ErrMigrationV4Explicit (explicit-preview gate pinned through adoption test).\\n+- VALIDATION (head a89328c): gofmt clean; go vet ./... clean; GOOS=windows build hosttrust+config ok; go build ./... ok; go test ./... -count=1 26/26 ok; -cover config 93.2 hosttrust 77.0 peeridentity 97.5 secprim 94.4; tracecheck ok (63/36/101/32, clauses 17/463); catalog v0.6.0 -check ok (former gate-21 input present). Mutation batteries rerun on new base: hosttrust 15 narrowing killed + neutral passed; config 4 narrowing killed + neutral passed; manifests bound to a89328c in mutations-hosttrust-refresh/ and mutations-config-refresh/.\\n+- PRESERVATION: RPC backup 15/15 manifest match; parked 11/11 match; tracked RPC paths clean; no rpcwire/UNRESOLVED remnants; RPC delta absent from candidate. Worktree left UNCOMMITTED for snapshot; no main push/integration (orchestrator step).\\n+\\n+## 2026-09-10 (later)\\n+\\n+### TASK-260909-2ez769 retry — closed-reader hardening + mutation refresh\\n+- SCOPE: same candidate; new gates only in `internal/hosttrust` + 1 census row. No config-package behavior change.\\n+- FINDING: `DecodeTrust` never bound identifiers to bytes (crafted/corrupt store with swapped digests decoded) and never checked cross-entry leaf/key/root uniqueness at read time; fixed in `trust_decode.go`/`trust.go` with 5 new refusal rows.\\n+- FINDING: `MarkRetiring` (peer catch-up path) missed the no-later-than-old-leaf-expiry cap that `Rotate` enforces; added with `TestMarkRetiringCapsAtLeafExpiry`.\\n+- FINDING: `ValidateCustody` never bound the contained leaf to the credential directory name (valid credential filed under another name passed); added digest-vs-dir check with `TestValidateCustodyBindsDirectory`.\\n+- FINDING: old `unsorted entries` refusal fixture was malformed JSON (refused on shape, never reached the ordering check); replaced with a genuinely descending valid pair. The `>=`-to-`>` sort mutant stopped killing once the mapping gate subsumed identical entries; re-aimed to `==` (admits unsorted-but-distinct) killing via the genuine fixture.\\n+- FINDING: `AuthorizeDispatch` doc overclaimed same-lock check+dispatch; corrected to the actual guarantee (coherent check under shared lock; caller binds generation + watchdog; mutations use exclusive `WithMutationAuthorization`). Stale `transact` missing-store comment and `TOML/JSON` error comment fixed.\\n+- VALIDATION (this run): `go build ./...` 0; `go vet` touched pkgs 0; `gofmt` clean; `go test ./... -count=1` all ok; `go test ./... -cover` all ok (hosttrust 77.0%, config 93.2%, peeridentity 97.5%, secprim 94.4%); hosttrust harness 15 narrowing killed + neutral passed; config harness 4 killed + neutral passed; census + refusal-inventory green.\\n+- BLOCKER (unchanged, external): CR validation command 21/26 needs adoption files absent on story base c1eff01; `refresh-candidate` still refuses (\\\"requires the final unresolved leaf\\\"). No vendoring, no manual rebase. Candidate left UNCOMMITTED for snapshot.\\n+\\n+## 2026-09-10\\n+\\n+### TASK-260909-2ez769 — Host Trust Store 1.0.0 + Config 4.0.0 migration implemented\\n+- SCOPE: new `internal/hosttrust` (trust reader/writer, Profile-1 issuance/verify, custody, enroll/rotate/MarkRetiring/revoke, generation authz, export/exclusion); Config 4.0.0 reader/validator/encoder + Preview/Apply/Rollback in `internal/config`; v4 peeridentity interop test; secprim census extended to hosttrust.\\n+- FINDING: peer rotation catch-up had no local path (only self-rotation). Added `Store.MarkRetiring` with the same 24h/enrolled_at bounds. `ensureOwnerDir` verifies existing dirs, never repairs: silent narrowing masked a widened dir (caught by TestCustodyRefusals).\\n+- FINDING: Go x509 puts the CN ATV into Subject.Names (len 1), so CN-only means exactly one CN-OID ATV, not empty Names. Parsed-name check fixed in `profile_checks.go:subjectIsOnlyCN`.\\n+- FINDING: encoding/json decodes `\\\"1\\\"` into json.Number; generation now requires a bare JSON number. Duplicate JSON keys audited via token stream before decode.\\n+- DECISION: base refresh refused by tooling (\\\"candidate refresh requires the final unresolved leaf\\\"); no manual rebase. Candidate sits on c1eff01 citing v0.6.0 by value; adoption files not duplicated. Integration must land onto the adoption base.\\n+- VALIDATION: 21/21 AC rows driven; 11 hosttrust + 3 config narrowing mutants killed (named), 1 label-precision kill, 2 neutral controls; `go test ./...` all ok; config refusal-inventory + secprim census green.\\n+- STATUS: ready for review, worktree UNCOMMITTED for handoff snapshot.\\n+\\n ## 2026-09-09\\n \\n ### TASK-260908-2tkufa: recovered v0.6.0 consumer adoption and bound pending runtime owners\\n\",\n  \"original_output_bytes\": 7554,\n  \"original_output_tokens\": 1889,\n  \"truncated\": false\n}","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"bash","outcome":"success"}}}
