{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000d69f","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a08946-5fbe-7830-b2e8-af2616179f48"},"sequence":2474,"recorded_at":1780531400004943,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"b6e8a9ed-35e9-4191-9a50-1dfe1ff8a38f","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"b6e8a9ed-35e9-4191-9a50-1dfe1ff8a38f","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"b6e8a9ed-35e9-4191-9a50-1dfe1ff8a38f"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a08951-c348-7043-8063-6d52b8d85930"},"task_id":"01a08951-c348-7043-8063-6d52b8d85930","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a08951-c348-7043-8063-6d52b8d85930","chunk":"{\n  \"chunk_id\": \"exec-42-1\",\n  \"command\": \"grep -n \\\"subsum\\\" internal/config/refusal_inventory_test.go | head; echo ===; grep -rn \\\"config-refusal-subsumed\\\" internal/config/*.go | grep -v _test | head\",\n  \"description\": \"Find subsumption mechanism\",\n  \"exit_code\": 0,\n  \"terminal_status\": \"completed\",\n  \"output\": \"220:\\t\\t\\tif !strings.Contains(file.lines[position.Line-1], \\\"config-refusal-subsumed:\\\") {\\n===\\ninternal/config/loader.go:179:\\t\\treturn Inputs{}, loaderError(Error{Operation: \\\"capture working directory\\\", Err: errors.Join(ErrInvalidContext, err)}) // config-refusal-subsumed: os.Getwd has no injectable seam and does not fail on any supported host, including a cwd unlinked underneath the process, so this guard stays fail-closed and is pinned by the refusal-subsumption inventory\\ninternal/config/loader.go:229:\\t\\treturn Snapshot{}, loaderError(Error{Operation: \\\"read selected file\\\", Class: ConfigFile, Err: ErrInvalidContext}) // config-refusal-subsumed: ResolvePaths populates every overrideRegistry class, pinned by TestResolvePathsPopulatesEveryOverrideRegistryClass\\ninternal/config/loader.go:330:\\t\\t\\treturn loaderError(Error{Operation: \\\"inspect selected root\\\", Class: specification.Class, Err: ErrInvalidContext}) // config-refusal-subsumed: ResolvePaths populates every overrideRegistry class, pinned by TestResolvePathsPopulatesEveryOverrideRegistryClass\\ninternal/config/migration.go:230:\\t\\treturn result, migrationError(MigrationError{Operation: \\\"encode target\\\", Err: err}) // config-refusal-subsumed: every encoder refusal below this propagation is pinned on its own clause, at writer.go terminal.backend and writer.go v2 wire TOML for the v2 encoder, at writer.go v2 re-read for its defence-in-depth round trip, and by the EncodeCurrent validation suite for v3\\ninternal/config/migration_v4.go:175:\\t\\treturn preview, migrationError(MigrationError{Operation: \\\"encode target\\\", Err: err}) // config-refusal-subsumed: the preview pre-validates credential, enrollment, removals and source under the same context, so the v4 encoder admits only values its own clauses already accepted; any refusal here repeats a clause pinned above\\ninternal/config/schema.go:537:\\t\\treturn configError(\\\"closed TOML shape\\\", errors.Join(ErrConfigDecode, err)) // config-refusal-subsumed: envelope TOML syntax parse\\ninternal/config/writer.go:43:\\t\\treturn nil, configError(\\\"terminal.backend\\\", errors.Join(ErrConfigEncode, fmt.Errorf(\\\"cannot represent backend in Configuration %s\\\", Version2))) // config-refusal-subsumed: Migrate accepts Configuration 1.0.0 as the only v2 source and its closed reader admits only tmux or conpty\\ninternal/config/writer.go:60:\\t\\treturn nil, configError(\\\"TOML\\\", errors.Join(ErrConfigEncode, err)) // config-refusal-subsumed: v2 wire TOML - the v1 production reader supplies only closed scalar, slice, and map-free values to this private v2 wire encoder\\ninternal/config/writer.go:63:\\t\\treturn nil, errors.Join(ErrConfigEncode, err) // config-refusal-subsumed: v2 re-read - defence in depth only; the sole production caller is Migrate with a Configuration 1.0.0 source, whose closed reader has already validated every member this wire shape carries, so no valid v1 source can produce a v2 document this re-read refuses\\ninternal/config/writer.go:193:\\t\\treturn nil, configError(\\\"TOML\\\", errors.Join(ErrConfigEncode, err)) // config-refusal-subsumed: v4 wire TOML - the preview and the v4 validator admit only closed scalar values to this private v4 wire encoder, mirroring the legacy wire defence\\n\",\n  \"original_output_bytes\": 3187,\n  \"original_output_tokens\": 797,\n  \"truncated\": false\n}","final_result":true}}}
